    schema:datePosted "2026-08-18"^^xsd:date ;
    schema:description "Redefining Access to Private Markets Privatize is redefining access to Private Markets. Headquartered in Frankfurt, we aim to make top-tier Private Markets funds broadly accessible. We collaborate with renowned institutions like BlackRock, Carlyle, J.P. Morgan and Ares, enabling Private Equity, Private Debt, and Real Asset investments through an innovative Fintech infrastructure. Aufgaben Objective of the Role Are you interested in a career in Private Equity, Strategy Consulting or Asset Management and looking to gain meaningful experience in the Private Markets space? As a Corporate Development & Growth Intern, you will work closely with our leadership team to support strategic initiatives across investor engagement, financial analysis, and business development. You will contribute to high impact projects such as the development of new product strategies, investor materials, strategic growth, and market research, while gaining exposure to the dynamics of the broader Private Markets ecosystem. Your Responsibilities Take ownership of strategic projects alongside the leadership team, working with top-tier Asset Management partners Conduct comprehensive market, product, and client research to deepen our knowledge base, identify growth opportunities, and support strategic planning Support the acquisition and onboarding of wealth managers, banks, and family offices through targeted outreach and structured project support Design and optimize dashboards, performance reports, and CRM workflows to enhance sales efficiency and data-backed decision-making Contribute to financial modelling and strategic analyses to drive sustainable revenue growth and support Privatize’s broader market expansion goals Qualifikation What We Are Looking For We are looking for a driven and analytical candidate with the following qualifications: Proficiency in both English and German is required Enrolled in a Bachelor's (4th semester or higher) or Master's program, or recently graduated in business, finance, economics, or a related field Strong interest in finance, ideally with a focus on Private Markets (e.g. Private Equity, Private Debt, Real Assets) Initial experience through internships in Start-Ups, Private Equity, Strategy Consulting, Venture Capital, Investment Banking, or similar environments Excellent analytical and communication skills; confident in using PowerPoint and Excel Benefits What you can expect from us Ownership & Impact: Lead initiatives that directly contribute to Privatize’s strategic development Collaboration & Learning: Work alongside a highly experienced team, gaining exposure to decision-making processes and senior stakeholders Growth & Development: Thrive in a learning-oriented environment that encourages curiosity, growth, and continuous development in the Private Markets space About Privatize At Privatize, we are redefining access to Private Markets by combining financial expertise with cutting-edge technology. As a fast-growing B2B2C Private Markets platform, we empower financial institutions, advisors, and investors with seamless solutions to navigate and invest in Private Markets funds. Our team is driven by a culture of innovation, collaboration, and excellence. We believe in fostering an environment where ambitious individuals can take ownership, push boundaries, and make a tangible impact on the future of finance. At Privatize, you’ll work alongside industry leaders and top-tier talent, tackling complex challenges while continuously growing your skills and career. Find more English Speaking Jobs in Germany on Arbeitnow" ;
