    schema:datePosted "2026-08-18"^^xsd:date ;
    schema:description "Please apply here: https://form.typeform.com/to/K45SsZ33 At Skinnify, we make clothing with built-in resistance — leggings, sleeves, shoes, and more — that turn everyday movements like walking, cooking, or commuting into a passive workout. In just three years, we've grown from 0 to 150,000+ customers – and we're just getting started. To get a better idea of our company and what it's like to work on our team, check out this short video:https://drive.google.com/file/d/1Imn7tqGmLXZxcpNBRI0mxYA6ayPwLT7j/view?usp=drivesdk Now, we're looking for a Full-Time Image Ad Designer (40 hours/week) to create world-class, high-converting creatives across paid advertising, email marketing, social media, our website, and other customer touchpoints. You'll play a key role in shaping our brand, improving conversion rates, and helping millions of women discover a new way to stay fit. Tasks ✅ Design high-converting static creatives for Facebook, Instagram, TikTok, Pinterest, Google Display, and other paid advertising platforms ✅ Create compelling landing page graphics, website banners, and promotional materials ✅ Design product visuals, mockups, packaging concepts, and marketing materials that align with our premium brand ✅ Work closely with creative strategists, copywriters, media buyers, video editors, and CRO specialists to bring campaign ideas to life ✅ Develop engaging social media content that strengthens Skinnify's brand presence ✅ Maintain and evolve our visual identity across all channels while ensuring brand consistency ✅ Organize design files, templates, and creative assets for efficient collaboration ✅ Continuously improve creatives based on performance data, A/B testing, and customer feedback Requirements ✔️ Proven Ad Design Experience - You’ve created successful ad images for e-commerce or DTC brands (fitness/fashion is a big plus) ✔️ DTC E-commerce Experience – Experience creating high-performing creatives for ecommerce brands (fashion, fitness, beauty, or consumer products is a big plus) ✔️ Advanced Design Software Skills – Proficient in Adobe Photoshop, Illustrator, Figma, or similar professional design tools ✔️ Performance-Driven Mindset – You understand that great design should not only look beautiful but also drive conversions ✔️ Creative Problem Solver – Able to translate marketing ideas into compelling visual concepts ✔️ Attention to Detail – Pixel-perfect execution with consistently high-quality work ✔️ Collaborative Yet Independent – Comfortable receiving feedback while taking ownership of your projects ✔️ Organized & Reliable – Able to manage multiple projects and consistently meet deadlines Benefits 📈 Join a Hyper-Growth Brand – From 0 to 150,000+ customers in 3 years. Your designs will directly influence our growth and customer experience. 🚀 Real Career Growth – Your trajectory here is whatever you make of it. One team member went from video editor to creative strategist and doubled their salary. Another started in customer support and now runs the entire customer support team. We promote from within and invest in people who want to grow. 💼 Full Flexibility – Work from anywhere, anytime. We run on trust and results, not time tracking—as long as the work gets done, your hours are yours. 🧠 Learning Budget – Courses, books, consulting calls—we cover it. Many team members book calls with founders of big ecommerce brands or managers at major companies through platforms ✈️ Two Company Retreats a Year, Fully Paid – We rent a house in a new country each time, explore, and actually get to know each other. Here is a video of our last company retreat: https://drive.google.com/file/d/1nOLkLRGauSxiJYMli4WxU36wJ5Z7aUe6/view?usp=sharing ⭐ Loved by the Team – Rated 5 out of 5 stars on Glassdoor 🏋️‍♀️ The Skinnify Story Our founder Christian grew up in Frankfurt, Germany. Looking around, he noticed something striking: so many of the women in his life — his mom, his sister, his friends — wanted to get fitter, lose weight, and build muscle, but kept running into the same wall. They didn't have the time, the motivation, or the consistency to make the gym work. The idea hit him during his own workout. He was using resistance bands and thought: what if these were built into everyday clothing? What if women could get the benefits of resistance training passively — while walking the kids to school, cooking dinner, or sitting at their desk? Fitness without the extra time or effort. The idea was personal too. Christian was a difficult kid growing up and put his mom through a lot. She barely had time for herself, let alone the gym. He built Skinnify for women like her: busy, hardworking, often overlooked — so they could do something good for their bodies just by getting dressed. 🛍️ Our Products What started with a single product — leggings with built-in resistance bands — has grown into a full collection of resistance-integrated clothing: leggings, sleeves, shoes, and more. We're on a mission to revolutionize how women do fitness by turning daily life into a workout. 🌟 Skinnify's Core Values 💡 Innovation – We design new, groundbreaking clothing with built-in resistance to revolutionize fitness. 🔥 Effectiveness – Our products help people burn more calories & get fitter with every step. 🌍 Accessibility – We make fitness accessible to everyone — even the busiest and least motivated. 🎉 Fun – We make exercise feel effortless and enjoyable. ✅ Quality – Our products are built to last — high-quality, durable, and reliable. Ready to design creatives that inspire millions and drive real business growth? Apply now and let's build the future of fitness together. Find more English Speaking Jobs in United Kingdom on Arbeitnow" ;
    schema:hiringOrganization kgjd:employer-skinnify ;
