    schema:datePosted "2026-08-14"^^xsd:date ;
    schema:description "Job Title: Knowledge Graph Architect Type: Contract Location – USA/ Canada – Remote Experience : 15+ years Job Summary We are looking for an experienced Enterprise Data & Knowledge Graph Architect to lead enterprise data modernization initiatives for an insurance client. This role will serve as a trusted advisor to senior stakeholders, driving enterprise architecture, semantic data modeling, knowledge graphs, and AI-enabled data solutions. The ideal candidate will design scalable enterprise data architectures, integrate with Duck Creek OnDemand, and enable GraphRAG-powered AI capabilities. Key Responsibilities Advise business and technology stakeholders on enterprise architecture and data modernization. Lead requirements gathering and translate business needs into scalable data architecture solutions. Design and implement enterprise ontologies, knowledge graphs, and semantic data models using RDF, OWL, and SPARQL. Architect graph database solutions using Neo4j, Microsoft Fabric Knowledge Graph, Amazon Neptune, or TigerGraph. Build GraphRAG architectures to support enterprise LLM and AI initiatives. Design integrations with Duck Creek OnDemand (Policy, Billing, and Claims) and enterprise integration platforms. Define Canonical Data Models and event-driven integration using Kafka or Azure Event Hubs. Requirements /Required Skills 10+ years of Enterprise/Data/Solution Architecture experience. Strong expertise in Knowledge Graphs, Ontologies, RDF, OWL, SPARQL, and Semantic Data Modeling. Hands-on experience with Neo4j/ Microsoft Fabric Knowledge Graph/ Amazon Neptune /TigerGraph. Experience with Master Data Management (MDM) and Enterprise Data Architecture. Knowledge of GraphRAG, LLM integration, and AI-driven data solutions. Experience with Duck Creek OnDemand and enterprise integration architecture. Strong understanding of Kafka, Azure Event Hubs, and event-driven architecture. Excellent stakeholder management and communication skills. Preferred Skills Knowledge of Duck Creek Integration Hub, Microsoft Fabric, and Azure Cloud. TOGAF or other Enterprise Architecture certifications. Experience with enterprise digital transformation and data governance. Regards, Manoj Goud Derex Technologies INC Contact : 973-834-5005 Ext 206 All your information will be kept confidential according to EEO guidelines. Derex Technologies Inc specializes in providing IT consulting, staffing solutions and software services. Globally headquartered in Harrison New Jersey since 1996 Derex delivers the highest quality technology professionals and an array of customized IT talent solutions designed to improve productivity and drive results to global clients throughout North America. With over two decades of unparalleled experience, Derex provides supports to its clientele, across such industries as Systems Integration, Banking and Finance, Telecommunications, Pharmaceutical and Life Sciences, Energy, Healthcare, Technology, Transportation, and local and federal Government agencies. Originally posted on Himalayas" ;
    schema:employmentType "Contractor" ;
    schema:experienceRequirements "Senior" ;
